This product bundles the hardware layer `rc-device` (repository: rc-device-sdk),
written from scratch by this project's author after reverse engineering the card
format and the serial protocol. It is original code, released under the same
license as the rest of this repository (MIT).

Its sources live in the separate repository `rc-device-sdk` and are included here
as a git submodule at `app/src-tauri/vendor/rc-device`. At build time it is
compiled into a 32-bit `rc-device-sidecar.exe` (the vendor driver is x86-only),
which the 64-bit application talks to over stdin/stdout NDJSON.

The vendor reader driver (LC32RFRW.dll) is shipped alongside for interoperability
with the hardware it was built for. It is not covered by this project's copyright
and no warranty of any kind is given for it.

